GRAPH REPRESENTATION:

====================================================================================================

ADJACENCY MATRIX:

====================================================================================================

1. IDEA

A graph with V vertices is stored as a V x V table.

+-------------+-----------------------------------------------+
| Cell value  | Meaning                                       |
+-------------+-----------------------------------------------+
| m[i][j] = 1 | Edge from i to j                              |
| m[i][j] = 0 | No edge                                       |
| m[i][j] = w | Weighted graph: weight is stored instead of 1 |
+-------------+-----------------------------------------------+

====================================================================================================

2. DIAGRAM

Graph:

        B
       / \
      A   D ---- E
       \ /
        C

Adjacency matrix:

        A  B  C  D  E
      +---------------+
    A | 0  1  1  0  0 |
    B | 1  0  0  1  0 |
    C | 1  0  0  1  0 |
    D | 0  1  1  0  1 |
    E | 0  0  0  1  0 |
      +---------------+

Row D = [0 1 1 0 1], so D is adjacent to B, C and E.

====================================================================================================

3. ARBITRARY VERTEX NAMES

The matrix only understands numbers, so keep two lookups:

+---------------+-----------+--------------+
| Lookup        | Structure | Example      |
+---------------+-----------+--------------+
| name -> index | Hash map  | "Delhi" -> 0 |
| index -> name | Array     | 0 -> "Delhi" |
+---------------+-----------+--------------+

Steps: convert the name to an index, work on the matrix,
then convert back when printing.

Cost: one extra O(1) average lookup per operation.

====================================================================================================

4. PROPERTIES

+------------------+----------------------------------------------------+
| Property         | Detail                                             |
+------------------+----------------------------------------------------+
| Space            | O(V^2): good for dense graphs, wasteful for sparse |
| Undirected graph | Matrix is symmetric                                |
| Directed graph   | Need not be symmetric                              |
| Self-loop        | A 1 on the diagonal                                |
| Degree           | Sum of the row (directed: row = out, column = in)  |
| Speed            | Edge lookup is fast, neighbour listing is slow     |
+------------------+----------------------------------------------------+

====================================================================================================

5. TIME COMPLEXITY

+---------------------------------+------------------------------------+
| Operation                       | Time                               |
+---------------------------------+------------------------------------+
| Check if u, v are adjacent      | O(1)                               |
| Find all vertices adjacent to u | O(V)                               |
| Find degree of u                | O(V)                               |
| Add an edge                     | O(1)                               |
| Remove an edge                  | O(1)                               |
| Add a vertex                    | O(V) amortized                     |
| Remove a vertex                 | O(V^2) naive, O(V) with swap trick |
| Space                           | O(V^2)                             |
+---------------------------------+------------------------------------+

Swap trick: copy the last vertex's row and column into the
removed slot, then shrink the matrix by one.

====================================================================================================

6. MATRIX VS LIST

+------------+------------------+----------------+
|            | Adjacency Matrix | Adjacency List |
+------------+------------------+----------------+
| Space      | O(V^2)           | O(V + E)       |
| Edge check | O(1)             | O(deg)         |
| Neighbours | O(V)             | O(deg)         |
| Best for   | Dense graphs     | Sparse graphs  |
+------------+------------------+----------------+
